{"question": "Vòng eo ở trẻ em có ý nghĩa gì trong việc đánh giá nguy cơ biến chứng chuyển hóa không?", "claim": "Vòng eo là một phép đo cụ thể về mỡ phần thân trên và được sử dụng để xác định trẻ thừa cân, béo phì có nguy cơ phát triển các biến chứng chuyển hóa.", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "Tài liệu lâm sàng ghi nhận số đo vòng eo giúp nhận diện trẻ thừa cân, béo phì đối mặt với nguy cơ biến chứng chuyển hóa."}], "conversation": {"history": []}, "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "Approximately 3% of extraoral halitosis cases are originated on the tonsils, due to caseum accumulation on their crypts. Caseums have a morphology similar to the dental biofilm (desquamated epithelial cells, keratin and food debris) colonised by anaerobic bacteria that produces VSCs, very similar to the tongue coating microbiota which can explain the mechanism leads to malodour. Bacterial sinusitis is the main cause of malodour exhaled though nasal cavity. Bacteria involved in mucus production are capable of directly producing VSCs."}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q2", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "It has been indicated that abdominal fat is one of the main reasons for the increased risk of death. Waist circumference is a specific measurement of upper body fat and has been used to identify overweight and obese children who are at risk of developing metabolic complications [41]. There have been few studies including waist circumference measurement in children [18, 42]. In the present study, in addition to height and weight assessment, waist circumference was also measured. Hatipoğlu et al., developed age and gender specific reference values for waist circumference in Turkish children between the ages of 7–17. They reported that waist circumference measurement increased with age and the waist circumference percentage values of boys at all ages were higher than girls [43]. Parallel results were also obtained in the present study. In a study investigating the relationship between anthr"}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q3", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "opometric measurements and dental caries in children aged 5–9 Turkey; an inverse relationship between waist circumference and DMFT was reported [18]. In another study in the 6–17 age group, BMI and waist circumference values were found to be significantly higher in children with a DMFT score of 0 than in children with a DMFT score > 1 [42]. In the present study, although the DMFT/DMFS index increased as waist circumference increased, the relationship was not significant. However, the inverse relationship between waist circumference and dmft/dmfs index was statistically significant. Additionally, as the waist circumference of the patients increased, the ICDAS II"}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "Drug-Related Halitosis: A Narrative Review", "heading_path": ["Body", "Introduction"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "Evaluation of the effect of obesity on oral health and halitosis in children", "heading_path": ["Body", "Discussion"]}]}
