{"question": "Thang đo OHIP-49 đánh giá bao nhiêu lĩnh vực chất lượng cuộc sống liên quan đến sức khỏe răng miệng?", "claim": "Thang đo OHIP-49 là một trong những công cụ toàn diện nhất, đánh giá tổng cộng bảy lĩnh vực bao gồm giới hạn chức năng, đau thể chất, khó chịu tâm lý, khuyết tật thể chất, khuyết tật tâm lý, khuyết tật xã hội và tàn tật với tổng số 49 mục.", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "Tài liệu hệ thống ghi nhận thang đo OHIP-49 bao gồm 49 mục đánh giá 7 lĩnh vực chất lượng cuộc sống liên quan đến sức khỏe răng miệng trên thang đo Likert 5 điểm."}], "conversation": {"history": []}, "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "Among various OHRQoL instruments, the OHIP-49 [82] is one of the most comprehensive. It evaluates seven domains: Functional limitation, physical pain, psychological discomfort, physical disability, psychological disability, social disability, and handicap, with a total of 49 items. Each item is rated on a 5-point Likert scale (0 = never, 1 = hardly ever, 2 = occasionally, 3 = frequently, 4 = very often). Higher scores indicate poorer OHRQoL. The Chinese version of OHIP-49 was translated by Sun Yat-sen University in 2011 and has demonstrated good reliability and validity in both community and patient populations. It is widely used and regarded as one of the most accurate instruments for evaluating OHRQoL. Shortened versions of OHIP-49 have also been developed to apply to different research settings."}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q2", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "Oral hygiene status was assessed in 14 (60.9%) of the 23 studies for association with the prevalence of dental caries. The Simplified Oral Hygiene Index (OHI-S) was the predominant tool, used in 12 (85.7%) of the studies [4,15,48,49,51–53,60–62,64,65], and one study used the Plaque Index [63]. Most studies that used the OHI-S reported the distribution of participants across categories of good, fair, and poor oral hygiene. One study did not specify its tool for OHI measurement [52], while another presented mean OHI-S scores stratified by urban/rural setting, gender, and age [53]."}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "Psychological factors and quality of life in oral mucosal diseases: A systematic review of assessment tools and clinical implications", "heading_path": ["Body", "Results", "Oral health-related quality of life instruments", "OHIP-49 (Oral Health Impact Profile-49)"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "Oral hygiene practices and dental caries experience in Nigeria: A systematic review and meta-analysis", "heading_path": ["Body", "Results", "Oral hygiene status, frequency, and devices used for oral hygiene", "Oral hygiene status assessment."]}]}
