{"question": "Tốc độ tăng sinh của tế bào gốc tủy răng (DPSCs) so với tế bào gốc trung mô tủy xương (BM-MSCs) như thế nào và do nguyên nhân gì?", "claim": "Tế bào gốc tủy răng (DPSCs) có tốc độ tăng sinh cao hơn khoảng 30% so với BM-MSCs, nhờ sự biểu hiện của các trung gian chu kỳ tế bào như cyclin-dependent kinase-6 và insulin-like growth factor.", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "Tài liệu nội bộ ghi nhận DPSCs tăng sinh nhanh hơn khoảng 30% so với BM-MSCs do tác động của các yếu tố chu kỳ tế bào như IGF và CDK-6."}], "conversation": {"history": []}, "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "DPSCs in the pulp have multidifferentiation potential and share the characteristics of MSCs.98 Hence, they play a vital role in maintaining homeostasis and tooth repair after birth by replenishing odontoblasts during dentin repair.99 Furthermore, they can play a vital role in the regeneration of damaged teeth.100 Dental stem cells share similarities with BM-MSCs, with similar surface markers and matrix proteins associated with mineralisation (alkaline phosphates, osteocalcin, and osteopontin).79,87,101"}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q2", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "Compared with BM-MSCs, DPSCs have a greater proliferation rate (∼30%), which can be attributed to the expression of cell cycle mediators such as cyclin-dependent kinase-6 and insulin-like growth factor in DPSCs.102 Dental pulp-derived stem cells are able to differentiate into odontoblastic (dentin-forming), osteoblastic (bone-forming), neurogenic (nerve-forming), adipogenic (fat-forming), myogenic (muscle-forming), chondrogenic (cartilage-forming), and melanocytic (pigment-forming) cell lineages in vitro. They are also able to form a mineralised matrix resembling dentin or bone and exhibit neurotrophic (nerve-feeding) properties when transplanted into immunodeficient mice.79,101,103"}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "Dental Pulp Stem Cells for the Management of Plaque Biofilm-Associated Infections : A Review", "heading_path": ["Body", "Methods", "Mesenchymal stem cell therapy", "Properties and functions of DPSCs"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "Dental Pulp Stem Cells for the Management of Plaque Biofilm-Associated Infections : A Review", "heading_path": ["Body", "Methods", "Mesenchymal stem cell therapy", "Properties and functions of DPSCs"]}]}
