et al. 2023). All five papers received a score of between 7 and 9, indicating high quality and low risk of bias (Al Deeb et al. 2020a, 2020b; Al‐Hamoudi et al. 2020; ALharthi et al. 2019;"}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "Diagnosis-based pathways for conservative and minimally invasive management of temporomandibular disorders: a scoping review", "heading_path": ["Body", "3. Result", "3.5 Risk of bias assessment"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "Effect of Vaping on Treatment Outcomes in Patients With Gingivitis, Periodontitis, and/or Peri‐Implant Disease: A Systematic Review", "heading_path": ["Body", "Results", "Quality Assessment of Included Studies"]}]}
