{"question": "Đối tượng bệnh nhân nào được đưa ra trong tiêu chí lựa chọn nghiên cứu về hiệu quả của việc loại bỏ mảng bám cơ học chuyên nghiệp trong điều trị viêm nướu?", "claim": "Đối tượng nghiên cứu bao gồm quần thể người lớn hoàn toàn hoặc một phần bị viêm nướu do mảng bám răng tự nhiên trên mô nha周期 nguyên vẹn hoặc bị giảm mà không có tiền sử viêm nha chu.", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "Tài liệu hệ thống hóa đối tượng nghiên cứu là người trưởng thành mắc viêm nướu do mảng bám trên nền nha chu nguyên vẹn hoặc đã tiêu xương nhưng không có tiền sử viêm nha chu."}], "conversation": {"history": []}, "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "TABLE 1"}, {"quote_id": "P1.Q2", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "This is a table summarizing the mechanism of action of the above natural anti-inflammatory drugs."}, {"quote_id": "P1.Q3", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "Medicine | Anti-inflammatory mechanism | Reference"}, {"quote_id": "P1.Q4", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "Ginkgolide B | Regulate NF-κB p65 subunit translocation, IκB-α phosphorylation, IKK-β activity, inflammatory cytokines and proteins expression mediated by zinc finger protein A20, and LPS-induced MAPK pathway activation | (Li et al., 2009; Chu et al., 2011; Zhang et al., 2011 , 2018; Hu et al., 2018)"}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q5", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "Population: Adult populations consisting entirely or partly of subjects with naturally occurring dental biofilm–induced gingival inflammation on an intact or reduced periodontium in the absence of a history of periodontitis (e.g., traumatic gingival recessions), potentially including some periodontitis patients with maximum clinical attachment level (CAL) ≤ 3 mm or a maximum distance between the cemento‐enamel junction (CEJ) and the alveolar bone crest of ≤ 4 mm (if CAL was not assessed). A degree of flexibility was applied, whereby studies were considered eligible even when explicit reference to the participants' baseline diagnosis was not included among the inclusion criteria. In such cases, the study population comprised young adults, with no specific mention of periodontitis, yet the baseline inflammatory condition of the gingival tissues—although not explicitly listed as an inclusio"}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q6", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "n criterion—was clearly described in the Results section of each study. Studies were excluded when dealing with experimentally induced gingivitis if they did not explicitly report either the age range or the baseline conditions of the periodontal support of the participants, if they were performed exclusively on periodontitis cohorts or if they were performed on cohorts consisting partly or entirely of periodontitis patients with CAL > 3 mm and/or distance CEJ–bone crest > 4 mm at any site;"}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "Bioceramic bone tissue-engineered substitutes with anti-inflammatory effects in periodontitis", "heading_path": ["Body", "Bioactive anti-inflammatory molecules", "Natural anti-inflammatory molecules", "Resveratrol"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "Clinical Efficacy of Interventions Based on Professional Mechanical Plaque Removal in the Treatment of Dental Biofilm–Induced Gingivitis: A Systematic Review and Meta‐Analysis", "heading_path": ["Body", "Materials and Methods", "Study Selection Criteria"]}]}
