{"question": "Viêm xoang hàm do nguyên nhân răng có thường bị bỏ sót hoặc đánh giá thấp trước khi xuất hiện các triệu chứng nha khoa rõ ràng không?", "claim": "Viêm xoang hàm do răng (ODS) thường khá bị bỏ sót, đánh giá thấp và bị phớt lờ cho đến khi có các yếu tố liên quan đến răng miệng rõ ràng và đáng kể xuất hiện.", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "Tài liệu nội bộ ghi nhận tình trạng viêm xoang hàm do răng thường không được chẩn đoán kịp thời và bị bỏ qua cho tới khi triệu chứng răng miệng bộc lộ rõ."}], "conversation": {"history": []}, "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "Figure 2 It might seem unusual, however, sometimes the correlation between dental-related radiolucent areas in the tooth-bearing structures might be easily misdiagnosed because of the variation in the alveolar recess depth, presence of Underwood septa, some anatomical variations in the bone shape of the maxillary sinus, or the condition of the underlying bone [8,9,10,11,12,13,14,15]. The so-called odontogenic sinusitis (ODS) is quite often neglected, underrated, and frequently ignored until some other obvious improved and significant tooth-related factors are present. It is also worth remembering that small lesions with uncertain behavior in the tooth periapical or periodontal area might cause ODS appearances in various stages. The scheduled CT revealed a complete lack of ventilation of the right maxillary sinus, followed by total opacity, with fluid-like and polyp mass formation extendi"}, {"quote_id": "P1.Q2", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "ng towards the nasal cavity in between the inferior and middle conchae (blue arrow) [15,16,17,18,19,20,21]. In Figure 2, the space under the lower conchae and the nasal septum remains partially blocked and covered by the nasal polyps and some sinus secretion. Red arrows (A,C,D) show active periapical lesions with cystic formation because of advanced dental caries ((B) yellow arrow). Adjacent to the mentioned"}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q3", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "Table 1"}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q4", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "Teachers' knowledge, experience, and management regarding TDIs—comparison between Bengaluru and Chennai centers"}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q5", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "Questions | Response | Bengaluru | Chennai | p-value"}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q6", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "N | % | N | %"}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q7", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "Do not know | 40 | 33.1 | 45 | 37.5"}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q8", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "Statistically significant p-values (p < 0.05) are shown in bold"}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "Odontogenic Sinusitis: The Selective Role of a Modified Caldwell–Luc Approach in Two CT/CBCT-Documented Cases", "heading_path": ["Body"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "Assessment of Schoolteachers' Knowledge and Experience in the Emergency Management of Traumatic Dental Injuries: A Two-center Cross-sectional Study", "heading_path": ["Body", "Results"]}]}
